Hi Ryan.
Sounds like you're doing pretty good.  Here's my advice for the next
few tasks.

1)  Assuming you've hit minetown already, I would consider doing
sokoban before finishing the mines.  Even with a powerful character
like yours the mines can be dangerous, and sokoban has plenty goodies
that can help you (most notebly if you get lucky and find an amulet at
the last level).  Besides, your quest artifact is a luckstone, so you
don't really need to complete the mines at all.  That said, if you're
only one or two levels from the bottom, you may as well finish it up
(don't be afraid to retreat and come back later if you see something
that looks remotely dangerous).

2)  This is connected to the previous point, but while MR is most
important, reflection should be the next issue on your list.  This
protects you (and your equipment) against various wands
(sleep/lightning/fire), dragon breath and YASD from walking into
floating eyes (just happend to me).

3)  Your two-handed axe is a pretty good weapon, but there are other,
better weapons out there.   If nothing else, consider that using a
one-handed weapon will allow you to use a shield, and furthermore, as a
barbarian, you can wield two (one handed) weapons at once (and *really*
dish out damage).  I would at least experiment a bit.

4) Even though your character has the potential to dish out a large
amount of damage in hand to hand combat, I would suggest carrying
around a stash of throwable weapons, in case you meet something you're
not sure of or need to take out from afar.  Besides, why  get hit at
all when you can throw stuff at monsters before they even get close.

5)  You could use some improvments in your armor.  You say that you
have magic marker(s).  I would bless them and write blessed scrolls of
enchant armor.  You're going to be wearing that cloak of MR to the end
of the game, might as well enchant it up (never try to enchant a
non-elven piece of armor that is already +4 or more).

6) Another way to improve the armor class is by donating to the priest.

7) Magicbane is a handy item to have around, even if you're not going
to wield it.  You can use it for making a decently permenant 'E' word
in one turn.  As a barbarian, you don't need it as much, but I would
get into the habit of engraving it at every downstairs/ under random
piles of rocks, etc.

8) Once you're done with the mines and sokoban, keep going down in the
main dungeon until you hit Medusa's level, and then decide if you're
ready to do the quest.

Happy Hacking.
